==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/tʌt͡ʃt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-touched.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌtʃt|s=1}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Emotionally [[moved]] (by), made to feel emotion (by).
#: {{ux|en|I was '''touched''' that he should remember my birthday.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1845|author=[[w:Benjamin Disraeli|Benjamin Disraeli]]|title=[[s:Sybil/Book 4/Chapter 1|Sybil]]|section=Book 4, Chapter 1
|passage="They say her Majesty is more '''touched''' about these affairs of the Chartists than anything else," said Mr Egerton.}}
#* {{RQ:Alcott Little Women|chapter=[[s:Little Women/Chapter 42|Chapter 42: All Alone]]|text=“If there is anything good or true in what I write, it isn’t mine. I owe it all to you and Mother and Beth,” said Jo, more '''touched''' by her father’s words than by any amount of praise from the world.}}
#* '''1883''', [[w:Jules Verne|Jules Verne]], Mary de Hauteville (translator), ''[[s:The Green Ray/Chapter XXI|The Green Ray]]'', Chapter XXI: A Tempest in a Cavern,
#*: “And you came to save me, Mr. Oliver,” answered Miss Campbell, more '''touched''' by the courage of the young man than the dangers which could still happen.
# Slightly mentally deficient; [[touched in the head]].
#* '''1913''', [[w:Fyodor Dostoevsky|Fyodor Dostoevsky]], Eva M. Martin (translator), ''[[s:The Idiot/Part III/Chapter IV|The Idiot]]'', Part III, Chapter IV,
#*: "Don't you see he is a lunatic, prince?" whispered Evgenie Pavlovitch in his ear. "Someone told me just now that he is a bit '''touched''' on the subject of lawyers, that he has a mania for making speeches and intends to pass the examinations. I am expecting a splendid burlesque now."
#* {{RQ:Joyce Ulysses|chapter=Episode 8: The Lestrygonians|passage=All a bit '''touched'''. Mad Fanny and his other sister Mrs Dickinson driving about with scarlet harness.}}

